      "text": "Mimori is a data-extortion / ransomware group first observed on 2026-10-20, when it launched a leak site and listed its first two claimed victims: OpenText (Canada, technology) and AVEVA (UK, industrial software), claiming 177,234 files from AVEVA. A third claimed victim, St. James's Place (UK, financial services), was reported on 2026-10-21. The leak site, mimori.group, is a clearnet domain fronted by Cloudflare that publishes victim pages under /organizations/<victim> and threatens to publish stolen data unless victims make contact. None of the claims has been independently verified. AVEVA and OpenText have each disclosed a separate security incident (unauthorized access to AVEVA's..."
